```java
@Service
public class CacheService {

    @Autowired
    private DataSource dataSource; // injected after constructor

    @PostConstruct
      public void init() {
        // safe to use dataSource here
        loadInitialCache(dataSource);
    }

    @PreDestroy
    public void cleanup() {
        // release resources before shutdown
        clearCache();
    }
}
```

**Tight coupling** (without IoC):
```java
public class OrderService {
    private EmailService emailService = new EmailService(); // tightly coupled
}
```
Changing `EmailService` constructor requires changing `OrderService`.

**Loose coupling** (with IoC + interface):
```java
public class OrderService {
    private final NotificationService notificationService;

    public OrderService(NotificationService notificationService) {
        this.notificationService = notificationService;
    }
}
```
Spring injects `EmailService` (which implements `NotificationService`). To switch to SMS, inject `SmsService` — `OrderService` changes zero lines.

```java
// Method 1: @Autowired (simplest)
@Service
public class MyService {
    @Autowired
    private ApplicationContext applicationContext;

    public void doSomething() {
        MyBean bean = applicationContext.getBean(MyBean.class);
    }
}

// Method 2: ApplicationContextAware (explicit contract)
@Component
public class MyComponent implements ApplicationContextAware {
    private ApplicationContext ctx;

    @Override
    public void setApplicationContext(ApplicationContext ctx) {
        this.ctx = ctx;
    }
}
```
